A||||5||DISenchanted||Brake Calipers||||1
Z||000000||DISenchanted||10-14-1999||07:48 PM||||How hard is it to rebuild Brake Calipers?  Anyone tried?  Got any hint's that might make it easier.  What all do I need?  I'm flying blind here.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-14-1999||07:59 PM||||unless you have someone that does this allot to help you then don't do it. As I've said in other posts.... Disk brake calipers are not simple things to rebuild and not have leak. Especially rears with E-brake arms. The design of the caliper is basically simple, but it's reliable operation requires very small tolerances.<P>1. the bores need to be checked for damage, out of round, and bore diam. Unless you are replaceing the pistons they too must be check for damage and wear.<P>2. assuming the bores are decent to start with you then hone the bores. This alone is an art form. Do it wrong and you're guaranteed a leak.<P>3. then you check bore roundness, and diameter again. If the dimensions are too large then the caliper has to be scrapped.<P>4. after all that, you have to assemble the things extremely carefully. A single small nick or scratch and the thing is likely trash.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Andy||10-14-1999||08:23 PM||||I agree with theogre.I had to replace my calipers a few month ago.I found a rebuild kit,[I think the fiero store sells them].But I decided to call Advance Auto store and check how much a new one cost.Buy the time I purchased the new one and got my core charge back,I ended up spending about $15 more and had a new one.It was worse the difference not to have to go threw all the headaches that come with one ,you try to rebuild youre self.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||10-14-1999||11:58 PM||||I would be careful with the rebuilt calipers from Advance Auto. I had to take the right rear caliper on my car back 3 times before I got one that did not leak. They were pretty nice the first couple of times, but the last time they acted like it was my fault and said that they were only obligated to replace it once, then it was my problem. I think it has a lot to do with the store manager, but I have not been back to find out.||||reg||13
Z||000004||g2||10-15-1999||02:07 AM||||Check out the local parts houses, I replaced a stuck caliper on my son's Fiero a couple week's ago with a rebuilt from O'Reilly for about $18, with a lifetime warranty.||||reg||12
Z||000005||Andy||10-15-1999||08:36 PM||||Cooter,sorry you have had problems with you're  parts from Advance ,I bought mine and havent had no problems so far.I guess I was lucky.But most cities have more than one auto store,so I would call around and check for prises .||||reg||1
